    <string name="setting_eraser_end">Preview the eraser end</string>
    <string name="setting_eraser_end_detail">The display draws the eraser end’s track at once while you erase, and Nib erases when you lift. Off: the page updates as you erase, more slowly.</string>
    <string name="settings_pen">Pen</string>
    <string name="settings_fingers">Fingers</string>
    <string name="settings_panels">Panels</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_detail">Cards you drag stay where you leave them, separately in portrait and landscape.</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_reset">Put every card back beside its key</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_done">Every card is back beside its key</string>
    <string name="settings_preview">Display preview</string>
    <string name="setting_marker_preview">Marker and highlighter preview</string>
    <string name="setting_marker_preview_detail">This display can’t show a see-through preview in most colours, so the preview is either see-through or in colour.</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_grey">See-through grey</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_grey_detail">A translucent grey as light as your colour. What’s under the stroke stays visible, and the colour appears when you lift the pen.</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_solid">Solid colour</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_solid_detail">Your colour, roughly (blue shows as grey), covering what’s under the stroke until you lift the pen. Very pale colours may not show.</string>
    <string name="settings_preview_detail">If the display’s preview while you draw looks wider or thinner than the stroke that replaces it, match the two in Diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="setting_straight">Hold to draw a straight line</string>
    <string name="setting_straight_detail">Rest the pen at the end of a stroke for half a second and the stroke becomes a straight line from where it began. On the tablet, the display previews the stroke as drawn; the straight line replaces it when you lift.</string>
    <string name="setting_left_handed">Tools on the right</string>
    <string name="setting_left_handed_detail">For drawing with the left hand: the pens, tools and sliders move to the right edge.</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_drawing">Draw with a finger</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_drawing_detail">Off: fingers only move the page, and the pen is the only thing that draws.</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_pan">One finger moves the page</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_pan_detail">When fingers don’t draw. Two fingers always pinch, move and turn it.</string>
    <string name="setting_fast_gestures">Fast refresh while things move</string>
    <string name="setting_fast_gestures_detail">The display’s quick mode while fingers pan, zoom or turn the page, and while you drag a selection, as in BOOX’s own apps. It cleans up the screen once you stop.</string>
    <string name="setting_palm_guard">Palm guard</string>
    <string name="setting_palm_guard_detail">The display ignores fingers on the canvas while the pen is near, so a resting hand can’t move the page. Not yet tested on this tablet: try it in Diagnostics › Lab first.</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal">Show the finished ink</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal_detail">While you write, the display draws its own quick preview of each stroke; Nib’s finished ink replaces it.</string>
    <string name="reveal_auto">Auto</string>
    <string name="reveal_auto_detail">At breaks for the pens the display previews faithfully, after a pause for textured, blended and see-through ones.</string>
    <string name="reveal_breaks">At breaks</string>
    <string name="reveal_breaks_detail">As BOOX Notes does: when you touch a control, open a panel, move the page or undo. Quick writing stays quickest.</string>
    <string name="reveal_pause">After a pause</string>
    <string name="reveal_pause_detail">Once the pen rests, Nib puts its exact ink on the display without interrupting you.</string>
    <string name="reveal_every">After every stroke</string>
    <string name="reveal_every_detail">As Nib 0.2 did: each stroke is replaced when you lift the pen, which slows quick writing.</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal_pause">Pause before the finished ink</string>
    <string name="setting_gestures">Tap with two fingers to undo, with three to redo. Fingers are ignored while the pen is near the screen.</string>

