    <!-- Diagnostics › Lab -->
    <string name="diag_lab">Lab</string>
    <string name="diag_lab_help">The display calls Nib now relies on that haven’t been seen working on this tablet yet. Try each one, then answer; the answers go into Nib’s log.</string>
    <string name="lab_push_ink">Push ink</string>
    <string name="lab_push_controls">Push controls</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_end">Eraser end</string>
    <string name="lab_lasso">Lasso</string>
    <string name="lab_fast_mode">Fast mode</string>
    <string name="lab_palm_guard">Palm guard</string>
    <string name="lab_style_params">Style settings</string>
    <string name="lab_limit">Limit</string>
    <string name="lab_fed_stroke">Fed stroke</string>
    <string name="lab_pen_state_4">Pen state 4</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_painters">Eraser painters</string>
    <string name="lab_geometry">Geometry</string>
    <string name="lab_clean_screen">Clean screen</string>
    <string name="lab_push_ink_help">Draw a stroke in a band, then rest the pen for %1$s. Nib pushes its own finished ink to the display without letting a frame through. Did the preview become Nib’s exact stroke?</string>
    <string name="lab_push_controls_help">Draw several strokes without touching anything else. The counter is pushed to the display after each one while the display holds Nib’s frames. Did it keep up?</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_end_help">Draw a few strokes, then turn the pen round and rub them out with the eraser end. The display is asked to draw the eraser’s track itself; Nib erases when you lift.</string>
    <string name="lab_lasso_help">Draw a loop in the lasso band. The display is asked to draw the path as a dashed line, which goes when you lift.</string>
    <string name="lab_fast_mode_help">Draw something, then drag the surface with a finger: once with fast mode on, once with it off. The grid moves with it.</string>
    <string name="lab_palm_guard_help">Turn Palm guard on, hold the pen just above the surface and rest your hand on it. While the pen is near, finger touch should be off over the surface. If fingers still do nothing a second after you take the pen away, answer Stuck off.</string>
    <string name="lab_style_params_help">The fountain style’s own settings, sent to the display as you set them. Draw after each change: does the preview’s response to pressure change? The display’s own values are put back when you leave.</string>
    <string name="lab_limit_help">The preview is limited to the middle band, given in screen coordinates. Draw across all three bands.</string>
    <string name="lab_fed_stroke_help">Nib pauses the preview and feeds a line of points across the middle of the surface to the display’s own width model. Watch the surface as you press the key.</string>
    <string name="lab_pen_state_4_help">The surface opens its session, then Nib asks the display to hold pen state 4, which the firmware names erasing but never sends itself. Draw with the tip: does the display preview anything, and what does it read back (in the log)?</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_painters_help">Each band sets another eraser painter, 0 at the top to 8 at the bottom. Rub with the eraser end in every band and answer per band whether its track showed.</string>
    <string name="lab_geometry_help">What the display reports about its own geometry for the way the tablet is turned now. Turn the tablet and read again.</string>
    <string name="lab_clean_screen_help">The two ways BOOX’s reader cleans a colour screen. Try each one and say how it looked.</string>
